; c[idx[i]] = muladd(w[i], z, c[idx[i]]) for complex doubles, with z loop-invariant.
; The two-lane instruction-count veto credits the scalar code with fusing each
; FMul into its FAdd/FSub. With FMA, the vector FMul fuses with the alternating
; FSub/FAdd too (FMADDSUB), so the tree must vectorize with FMA as it does
; without.
